{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And clean and righteous — do not kill.</b> From where do we learn that if one goes out of court guilty and someone says, 'I have grounds to argue in his favor,' they return him to court? Scripture says: וְנָקִי אַל תַּהֲרֹג — and even though he is not 'righteous,' for he was not vindicated in court, nevertheless he is נָקִי — clear from the death penalty, since you have grounds to vindicate him. And from where do we learn that if one goes out of court acquitted and someone says, 'I have grounds to argue against him,' they do not return him to court? Scripture says: וְצַדִּיק אַל תַּהֲרֹג — and this one is 'righteous,' for he was vindicated in court (Sanhedrin 33)." "<b>For I will not justify the wicked.</b> It is not upon you to return him, for I will not justify him in My justice — if he escaped your hand as acquitted, I have many agents to put him to death by the death penalty he incurred (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:04.418994499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}